      "summary": "The implementation otherwise addresses the scoped identity, telemetry privacy, and alert requirements. The review endpoint currently emits a misleading investigation completion event for reviews that ran no investigation.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Auth/CaseEndpoints.cs",
          "line": 69,
          "message": "The review endpoint labels a non-investigation as investigation.completed. Emit a review event here, or emit investigation.completed only when an investigation actually ran.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "After a review is recorded, RecordReview emits an investigation.completed event with model set to \"not-invoked\" and empty tool and citation lists, although this endpoint runs no investigation.",
            "failureScenario": "A successful human review with no investigation produces a trace that downstream consumers can interpret as a completed investigation, with placeholder model and correlation data. The issue's scope notes say this endpoint is not expected to carry a real investigation trace."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
      "reviewType": "testing",
      "harness": "codex",
      "harnessVersion": "0.162.0",
      "model": "gpt-6-luna",
      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The tests cover the app grants, telemetry reader, trace helpers, and alert routing. They do not verify that the migration and Terraform identities retain their specified scopes, so a widened assignment can pass the M-14 tests.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/identity-telemetry.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 300,
          "message": "M-14 tests do not detect widened scopes for the migration or Terraform identity.",
          "confidence": 0.86,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The M-14 migration identity test checks the role name and SQL server name, but does not assert the migration role assignment's scope. The other M-14 tests also do not verify the Terraform identity's scope.",
            "failureScenario": "If migration_sql.scope is widened from the SQL server to the resource group while its role and server resource remain unchanged, these assertions still pass, although M-14 requires the migration and Terraform identities to retain their specified scopes."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
